                                  2.0 General
                                  ~~~~~~~~~~~

 2.1 Introduction
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This  software  packet is a complete chat replacement for TransAmiga BBS by
Sami  Radwan  and  Timothy   J.  Aston.  A  chat program allows the user to
communicate with the System Operator online.


Read  this  manual  carefully! It's the only way to prevent problems during
installation  and  usage.  If  you  encounter  any  problem you can't solve
yourself  write  a  message in a TransAmiga support echo or send netmail to
the address in the addenndum.


 2.2 Why Chat Wizard
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The  ChatWizard packet was developed as there was no comparable chat system
available  with similar possebilities. ChatWizard is always updated for new
TransAmiga releases.

Appart  from  the improved LineChat ChatWizard supports two different types
of split screen chats. They allow simultanious typing of SysOp and user.































        

        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                       page - 4


                                3.0 Installation
                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~


ChatWizard v2.0 and up include an installer script for easy setup.

Start the install-script from Workbench as any other WB program.

The  script  offers  a  variety  of  help texts accessible through the help
button. Read them if you are not sure about something.



 3.1 Configuration and later changes
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~


ChatWizard comes with three ARexx scripts:

ANSICustom.trans
ANSIWizard.trans
CChat.trans

ANSICustom.trans  and  CChat.trans  are  identical. They are thought to be
called from a menu as replacement of TransAmiga's internal chat.

The two scripts allow the following settings:

MODE=x  chooses  the type of chat. ChatWizard detects if ANSI is active and
chooses the chat type according to the following list:


 Mode | ANSI       | ASCII
------+------------+---------------------
   1  | AnsiWizard | LineWizard <default>
   2  | LineWizard | LineWizard
   3  | AnsiWizard | TA internal chat
   4  | LineWizard | TA internal chat




















        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                       page - 5


AMODE=x 
This selects the mode ANSIWizard is started with.

The following table lists the values and thier meaning:

 Mode | YellScript | ChatModus
------+------------+------------------------
   1  |  active    | horizontal splitting
   2  |  active    | vertical splitting
   3  |  inactive  | horizontal splitting <default>
   4  |  inactive  | vertical splitting


Other config entries:

Path=   <path to the main programs>
Config= <path and name of the config file>


The tables above are valid for ANSIWizard.trans as well. Just the following
options are used:


PATH=    <chatprogram path>
CONFIG=  <configfile path>
MODUS=   <startup mode - see table above>
CHATM=   In ASCII mode 0=LineWizard 1=TA internal chat
SPRACHE= language to use


For  integration  in  TransAmiga's  online  menu system you have to add the
following line to the corresponding .Rx file:


; ********************** *** ******************************
C ChatWizard             000 ANSIWizard.trans


For  the main menu you should change the chat entry in MAIN.CMDS. Give it a
key you never will use in your menu and set the access to 256.


 3.2 The commandline
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

AnsiWizard  and  LineWizard both can be invoked from a shell. The following
options can be used:


Syntax: ANSIWizard [-c<config file>] [-m<mode>] [-l<language>] [-n<line>]

This is the meaning of the options:

 -c path and name of the config file
 -m startup mode as listed above
 -l language
 -n BBS line

        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                       page - 6

                               4.0 Configuration
                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~


ANSIWizard  and LineWizard use the same config file. You can use a standard
text editor (Ed, MEmacs, Ged,...) for changes.

You  can  insert  comments  all  over  the script by starting a line with a
semicolon ;   The  program  recognizes  the  line  as  comment and does not
interpret it.


If  you  leave out an option the program uses internal default settings for
the corresponding part.


 4.1 The config file
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~


 4.1.1 COLORBGROUND, COLORB2GROUND
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

These commands let you choose the background colours.

Syntax: COLORBGROUND colour

         colour: The standard ANSI colour codes are used here. If the value
                 is too high or low internal defaults are used.



 4.1.2 COLORFGROUND
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This lets you choose the foreground colour.

Syntax: COLORFGROUND colour

         colour: The standard ANSI colour codes are used here. If the value
                 is too high or low internal defaults are used.



 4.1.3 COLORWRITE
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Here you select the colour which is used for user and sysop typing.

Syntax: COLORWRITE colour

         colour: The standard ANSI colour codes are used here. If the value
                 is too high or low internal defaults are used.






        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                       page - 7


 4.1.4 MAXLENGTH
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Specifies  the lines of the  sysop's local BBS window to prevent a garbeled
local screen if the user has more lines...


Syntax: MAXLENGTH lines

         lines: The  valid  range  is  20-60. If  the  range is exceeded an
                internal standard value is used.




 4.1.5 (NO)SCREENTOFRONT
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

As  soon  as  the  user  calls  the  sysop  TransAmiga's screen is made the
frontmost one.  This makes it easier for the sysop to answer the call. This
option is inactive for TransAmiga's internal chat.


Syntax: SCREENTOFRONT



 4.1.6 SYSOPNAME
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The  sysop  can  place his name here. It is displayed above his chat field.
With TransAmiga v1.1 and up the name is ordered from the BBS.


Syntax: SYSOPNAME "<NAME>"

          NAME: The name should not exceed 30 characters


 4.1.7  LINECOLORSYSOP
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Selects the colour for the text entered by the sysop.

Syntax:  LINECOLORSYSOP <colour>

         colour: The standard ANSI colour codes are used here. If the value
                 is too high or low internal defaults are used.










        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                       page - 8


 4.1.8  LINECOLORUSER
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Selects the colour for the text entered by the user.

Syntax:  LINECOLORUSER <colour>

         colour: The standard ANSI colour codes are used here. If the value
                 is too high or low internal defaults are used.




 4.1.9  LINEYELLSTRING
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Specifys the text displayed to the user when the chat is started.


Syntax:  LINEYELLSTRING "<text>"

           text: the text should consist of ASCII chars and not exceed
                 80 characters to prevent errors.



 4.1.10 (NO)LINEUSERBREAK
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This option enables or disables line chat termination by the user.




























        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                       page - 9


                               5.0 Script language
                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~


To  provide  the user with highest configuration and expansion capabilities
a script language has  been implemented.  You have full control on the call
function and can design your own environment. Several examples are included
in this archive.


If  you  do not use  your  own script  ChatWizard  uses  the  internal call
function.



 5.1 - Script commands
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This  section describes  the script commands in detail.  Scripts are inter-
preted  line by  line  starting  at the  first one.  Comment  lines  have a
semicolon (;) at the start of the line just like the config files.

The  KEY  commands  should  always  be  the first commands of a script. The
commands starting with KEY define the keymap and should be executed first.

The last command of a script should be YELLENDKEY.

Version 2.0 has no syntax checking. Unrecognized commands are just skiped.


 5.1.1 - BAR
 ~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: BAR <length> <time> <colour>

This  command  invokes  the  real  calling  of  the  sysop.  A bar is drawn
character  by  character.  With  each character a beep on the sysop side is
generated.

<length> is the length of the bar.  <colour> guess what - the colour of the 
bar.  <time> specifies  the seconds  between display of the segments of the
bar.


Example: BAR 14 1 6

A bar with 14 yellow  segments is drawn.  The segments are displayed with a
time delay of one second.










        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                      page - 10


 5.1.2 - BKCOLOR
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: BKCOLOR <colour>

BKCOLOR is the background colour for drawing (e.g. PRINT)




 5.1.3 - CLRLINE
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: CLRLINE <position> <ammount>

CLRLINE deletes <ammount> display lines starting at line <position>.



 5.1.4 - CLS
 ~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: CLS

CLS clears the whole screen.



 5.1.5 - COLOR
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: COLOR <colour>

Defines the foreground colour that should be used (e.g. for PRINT)




 5.1.6 - CONTINUE
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: CONTINUE

Checks for the return key.














        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                      page - 11



 5.1.7 - INPUT
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: INPUT <length> "<background>" <background_colour>

Asks  the user  why he  wants  to chat.  The line  he enters  is  stored in
TransAmiga's logfile.


<length>  is the length of the  user input.  <background> is the background 
char that is used  for input  text and gets the colour <background_colour>.
The character has to be enclosed in double quotes.




 5.1.8 - KEY-commands
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: KEYEXIT <character>
        KEYMESSAGE <character>
        KEYREPLAY <character>

The KEY commands define  the key mapping for the  command YELLENDKEY at the
end of the script.

KEYEXIT  is  the  character  the  user has to enter  if he wants  to return
to the BBS.

KEYMESSAGE is the character that invokes feedback.

KEYREPLAY  is  the character  that  restarts  the  script to yell the sysop
again.



 5.1.9 - LOADPIC
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: LOADPIC <path and filename>

LOADPIC  reads  an  ANSI  picture  and  displays  it  at the current cursor
location.


 5.1.10 - POSITION
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: POSITION <X> <Y>

Sets the curser to X, Y.






        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                      page - 12


 5.1.11 - PRINT, PRINTUSER, PRINTSYSOP
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: PRINT "<text>"
        PRINTUSER "<text>"
        PRINTSYSOP "<text>"

PRINT  displays  the  <text>  at  the current cursor position at the user's
and sysop's end.

PRINTUSER sends the <text> to the user only. The sysop does not see it.


PRINTSYSOP  dispalys  <text>  at  the  sysop's end only.  The user does not
see it.




 5.1.12 - SCREENTOFRONT
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: SCREENTOFRONT

Makes TransAmiga's screen the frontmost.



 5.1.13 - VERSION
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: VERSION

Displays the current version number and program name on the screen.




 5.1.14 - WAIT
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: WAIT <sec>

WAIT pauses for <sec> seconds.



 5.1.15 - YELLCOMMAND
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: YELLCOMMAND <path and filename>

Starts a DOS program with AmigaDOS RUN command.





        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                      page - 13



 5.1.16 - YELLENDKEY
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Syntax: YELLENDKEY

This  should  be  the  end  of  every  script. Everything that follows this
command  is never executed. If the sysop did not activate chat this command
asks  the  user  if he wants to retry, leave feedback or return to the BBS.
The KEY commands have to be used before this command!
















































        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                      page - 14


                           6.0 Function and usage
                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~


Version 2.0 offers not all functions that where planned.  This includes the
sysop menu within the chat. This function will come with v2.1.

CTRL-P shows the available control functions within the chat. A help window
is opened for the requesting side only. This function is available for both
sides.  The other side can continue typing. If the user calls this function
the sysop is informed by a little message.















































        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                      page - 15



                                  7.0  Addendum
                                  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 7.1  ANSI colour codes
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

ANSI  colour codes are the standard colours defined for ANSI. They are used
for eight colour screens and up.


   0  black
   1  red
   2  green
   3  yellow
   4  blue
   5  magenta
   6  Türkis
   7  white

These colours are valid for back- and foreground. Don't specify any numbers
out of range or you may encounter strange effects.

Invalid numbers are replaced by defaults usually.




 7.2  Examples
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~

example config file:

; config file for CHATWizard V2.0          (c) 1996 by TFB-Software
;
; Written by: Dietmar Zettel
;             Volker Braun
;
;
; system settings
;

SYSOPNAME "Dietmar Zettel"
COLORBGROUND 4
COLORFGROUND 6
COLORWRITE 7
MAXLENGTH 28
YELLFILE CHATWizard:YellProgramm/ChatYell02.prg

;
; special functions of LINEWizard
;

LINECOLORSYSOP 5
LINECOLORUSER 3
LINEYELLSTRING "Hi user, the sysop wants to chat..."
LINEUSERBREAK

        Chat Wizard Version 2.0 - Copyright (c) 1994-96 TFB-Software
  manual english               July, 24th 1996                      page - 16


example script file:

;----------------------------------
; YellProgramm 01  Grafix Work
;
; written by: Volker Braun
;----------------------------------

; key definitions for YellEndKey

KeyExit    e
KeyReplay  r
KeyMessage m

; screen design

CLS

LoadPic CHATWizard:YellPicture/ChatPic01.ANSI

; input for yell

color 6
position 12 37
input 42 "." 7

; yell the sysop

color 4
bkcolor 5
position 6 57
print "±±±±±±±±±±±±±±"
bkcolor 0

color 4
position 8 53
printuser "Press <CTRL X> to exit"
printsysop "Press <SPACE> to start"

position 6 57
bar 14 1 5

; yell script end

wait 1

position 6 60
bkcolor 5
color 0
print "finished"

wait 2






